course: dictionary
lesson: 4981
title: Indefinite: no fixed end
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indefinite means not fixed, not clear, or without an end. If something is indefinite, nobody has said exactly when, how many, or where it stops. «The library is closed for an indefinite time.» Nobody knows when it will open again, so the closure has no fixed end.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The answer was indefinite, so we still do not know what will happen.» The sentence tells you that an indefinite answer is one that is not clear or exact. Try your meaning in the sentence: "not clear" fits, so you are on the right track.
explain: Grammar uses the word too. «A» and «an» are called indefinite articles because they do not point to one specific thing: «a dog» could be any dog, while «the dog» means one particular dog.
explain: You will also meet the word in official writing. «"Detained at His Majesty's pleasure" is a British official phrase for being held in prison for an indefinite time, with no end date fixed in advance.» Here indefinite means no end date has been set.
fact: Indefinite means not fixed, not clear, or without an end or limit.
fact: «An indefinite stay» is a stay with no set end date.
fact: «Indefinitely» means for an unknown length of time, with no set end.
fact: «A» and «an» are indefinite articles; «the» is the definite article.
fact: «Indefinite» is the opposite of definite: definite means fixed, exact and clear.
exercise: «The shop is closed for an indefinite time.» What does indefinite mean here? | It is a very big shop | It is closed on Sundays only | It opens at nine o'clock every day | *No one knows when it will open
exercise: In grammar, which word is an indefinite article? | dog | *a | the | running
exercise: Which word means the opposite of indefinite? | Blurry | Vague | Endless | *Definite
test: «The bus will be late for an indefinite period.» What does indefinite tell you about the delay? | *It has no fixed end | It is a very fast bus | It will last exactly one hour | It will never happen
test: Which sentence uses an indefinite article? | I saw the film | I saw films | *I saw a film | I saw my film
exam: Mrs Khan says, «Her answer was indefinite.» What does she mean? | It was shouted loudly | It was a very long answer | It was clear and exact | *It was not clear or exact
